- **Guardrail: HELD — no same-day action.** auto's gen_pct was above control **every single day** of the 21-day unmonitored gap (recent-7d: 65.9% vs 17.8%). guided above control cumulatively and recent-7d (no sustained breach, just noisy days).
- guided's rage edge has **vanished** recent-7d (12.6% vs control 11.9%) — it is strictly dominated.
- **Decision: SHIP auto-capture — this is the 4th consecutive weekly read with the same verdict and it has STILL not been actioned.** ~1,700 flagged openers have been exposed to losing arms over 48 days. Evidence is at its strongest yet. Roll the flag to 100% auto-capture; retire guided and control. (If a strict frequentist 2-sided 95% on rage is required it's still a hair short, but the ship case rests on the 3× generation guardrail, which is overwhelming.)

## 2. tool-signup-cta-v2 (374737) — directional
- CTR/gen: control 27.0% | inline 28.7% | sticky 26.5%; signups 16 | 17 | 15 — **fully converged**; inline's early signup lead reverted during the gap (delta: control +7, inline +5, sticky +8).
- Guardrail **blind for the entire 7-week run**: `content_downloaded` = 0 events site-wide, `content_copied` = 25 events/12 users. Carried unfixed since wk1.
- **Decision: recommend CONCLUDE as a null result** (7 wks is well past the 2–3wk directional window) — ship inline-value-prop as permanent default (tiebreak: never below control) and retire the flag. Left as a human call per the don't-kill-post-signup rule. Fix the copy/download instrumentation before any successor CTA test.

